#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# none_true

#% text
# `none_true(xs, f)` is `true` when `f(x)` is `true` for no element `x` of `xs`.

#% text
# `none_true(xs, f, n)` tests the parts down to level `n`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# An empty list, or an atom, gives `true`.

#% item
# The values of an association are its elements.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
none_true([1, 3, 5], is_even)
#% output
#= true

#% cell
none_true([1, 2], is_even)
#% output
#= false

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# Down to level 2:

#% cell
none_true([[1, 3], [5, 7]], is_even, 2)
#% output
#= true

#% text
# The values of an association:

#% cell
none_true(assoc(a -> 1, b -> 3), is_even)
#% output
#= true

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `all_true`, `any_true`
